fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"codecparsers/gsth266parser.html#GstH266PPS","fragment":"\n\tGstH266PPS\n\nMembers\n\n\tGstCodecParsers.H266PPS\n\nMembers\n\n\tGstCodecParsers.H266PPS\n\nMembers\nStructure defining the H266 PPS.\nprovides an identifier for the PPS for reference by other\nsyntax elements.\nspecifies the SPS referred to by this PPS.\nthe GstH266SPS this PPS refers to.\nspecifies whether each picture referring to\nthe PPS has more than one VCL NAL unit and the VCL NAL units do not have\nthe same value of nal_unit_type.\nspecifies the width of each decoded picture\nreferring to the PPS in units of luma samples.\nspecifies the height of each decoded picture\nreferring to the PPS in units of luma samples.\nspecifies whether the conformance cropping window\noffset parameters follow next in the PPS.\nspecify left offset of the cropping window that\nis applied to pictures.\nspecify right offset of the cropping window that\nis applied to pictures.\nspecify top offset of the cropping window that\nis applied to pictures.\nspecify bottom offset of the cropping window that\nis applied to pictures.\nspecifies whether the scaling\nwindow offset parameters are present in the PPS.\nspecify the left offsets that are applied to the\npicture size for scaling ratio calculation.\nspecify the right offsets that are applied to the\npicture size for scaling ratio calculation.\nspecify the top offsets that are applied to the\npicture size for scaling ratio calculation.\nspecify the bottom offsets that are applied to\nthe picture size for scaling ratio calculation.\nspecifies whether the ph_pic_output_flag syntax\nelement could be present in PH syntax structures referring to the PPS.\nspecifies whether no picture partitioning is applied\nto each picture referring to the PPS.\nspecifies whether the subpicture ID mapping\nis signalled in the PPS.\nshall be equal to sps_num_subpics_minus1.\nshall be equal to sps_subpic_id_len_minus1.\nspecifies the subpicture ID of the i-th subpicture.\nspecifies the luma coding tree block size of each CTU.\nspecifies the number of explicitly provided\ntile column widths.\nspecifies the number of explicitly provided tile\nrow heights.\nspecifies the width of the i-th tile column in\nunits of CTBs.\nspecifies the height of the i-th tile row in units\nof CTBs.\nspecifies whether in-loop filtering\noperations across tile boundaries are enabled for pictures.\nspecifies whether the raster-san slice mode is in use for\neach picture referring to the PPS.\nspecifies whether each subpicture consists of\none and only one rectangular slice.\nspecifies the number of rectangular slices in\neach picture.\nspecifies whether all pictures are partitioned\ninto rectangular slice rows and rectangular slice columns in slice raster\norder.\nspecifies the width of the i-th rectangular\nslice in units of tile columns.\nspecifies the height of the i-th rectangular\nslice in units of tile rows.\nspecifies the number of explicitly provided slice\nheights for the slices in the containing the i-th slice.\nspecifies the height of the j-th rectangular\nslice in the tile containing the i-th slice.\nspecifies the difference between the tile index of the\ntile containing the first CTU in the (i+1)-th rectangular slice and the tile\nindex of the tile containing the first CTU in the i-th rectangular slice.\nspecifies whether in-loop filtering\noperations across slice boundaries are enabled.\nspecifies whether sh_cabac_init_flag is present\nin slice headers.\nspecifies the inferred value of the\nvariable NumRefIdxActive[0] for P or B slices.\nspecifies whether rpl_sps_flag[1] and rpl_idx[1] are\npresent in the PH.\nspecifies whether weighted prediction is applied to P\nslices.\nspecifies whether explicit weighted prediction is\napplied to B slices.\nspecifies whether the horizontal wrap-around\nmotion compensation is enabled.\nspecifies the difference between the\npicture width and the offset used for computing the horizontal wrap-around\nposition in units of MinCbSizeY luma samples.\nspecifies the initial value of SliceQp Y for each slice.\nspecifies whether either or both of the\nph_cu_qp_delta_subdiv_intra_slice and ph_cu_qp_delta_subdiv_inter_slice\nsyntax elements are present in PH.\nspecifies whether chroma tool offsets\nrelated syntax elements are present in the PPS.\nspecify the offsets to the luma quantization parameter Qp'Y\nused for deriving Qp'Cb.\nspecify the offsets to the luma quantization parameter Qp'Y\nused for deriving Qp'Cr.\nspecifies whether\npps_joint_cbcr_qp_offset_value and pps_joint_cbcr_qp_offset_list[i] are\npresent in the PPS.\nspecifies the offset to the luma quantization\nparameter Qp'Y used for deriving Qp'CbCr.\nspecifies whether the sh_cb_qp_offset\nand sh_cr_qp_offset syntax elements are present in slice headers.\nspecifies whether the\nph_cu_chroma_qp_offset_subdiv_intra_slice and\nph_cu_chroma_qp_offset_subdiv_inter_slice syntax elements are present in PH.\nspecifies whether number of\npps_cb_qp_offset_list[i], pps_cr_qp_offset_list[i],\nand pps_joint_cbcr_qp_offset_list[i], syntax elements that are present.\nspecify offsets used in the derivation of Qp'Cb.\nspecify offsets used in the derivation of Qp'Cr.\nspecify offsets used in the derivation of Qp'CbCr.\nspecifies whether presence of\ndeblocking filter control syntax elements in the PPS.\nspecifies whether the deblocking\nbehaviour could be overridden in the picture level or slice level.\nspecifies whether the deblocking filter is\ndisabled unless overridden for a picture or slice by information.\nspecifies whether deblocking filter information is\npresent in the PH syntax structure and not present in slice headers.\nspecify the default deblocking parameter offsets\nfor beta that are applied to the luma component.\nspecify the default deblocking parameter offsets for\ntC (divided by 2) that are applied to the luma component.\nspecify the default deblocking parameter offsets for\nbeta and that are applied to the Cb 